<servinfosub id = "AENLJA0A1134087003">
<title>
DTC Confirmation Procedure
</title>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
Check that the following condition is met in this “DTC Confirmation Procedure”.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Battery voltage &#62; 8.5 V
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</attention3>
<topic id = "AENLJA0A1134087004">
<title>
P2681 / P26B1
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Start engine when coolant temperature is 50 &#176;C (122 &#176;F) or lower.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Drive vehicle at 60 to 80 km/h (37 to 50 mile/h) for 10 min.
</ptxt>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Run engine at idle speed for 3 min.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</topic>
<topic id = "AENLJA0A1134087009">
<title>
P2682 / P2683
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Set ignition “ON” for 10 sec.
</ptxt>
</s1>
</topic>
</servinfosub>
<servinfosub id = "AENLJA0A1134087005">
<title>
DTC Troubleshooting
</title>
<diag type = "test" id = "AENLJA0A1134087006">
<testgroup id = "AENLJA0A1134087007">
<question>
Was “Engine and Emission Control System Check” performed?
</question>
<result type = "yes"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Go to Step 2.
</ptxt>
</action>
<result type = "no"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Go to 
<intxref refid = "AENLJA0A1134001">Engine and Emission Control System Check:K12D</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</action>
</testgroup>
<testgroup id = "AENLJA0A1134087008">
<title>
Coolant control valve actuator drive circuit check
</title>
<test1>
<ptxt>
Set ignition “OFF”, disconnect “C01” and “E01” connectors from ECM and coolant control valve connector.
</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>
Check for proper terminal connection to “C01” and “E01” connectors and coolant control valve connector.
</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>
If connections are OK, check the following points.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Resistance of “A1” and “A2” circuits: less than 1 &#937;
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Resistance between each of “A1” and “A2” circuits and ground: infinity
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Resistance between “A1” circuit terminal and other terminal at coolant control valve connector: infinity
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Resistance between “A2” circuit terminal and other terminal at coolant control valve connector: infinity
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Voltage of “A1” and “A2” circuits: approx. 0 V (When ignition is “ON”)
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</test1>
<question>
Is check result OK?
</question>
<result type = "yes"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Go to Step 3.
</ptxt>
</action>
<result type = "no"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Repair or replace defective wire harness.
</ptxt>
</action>
</testgroup>
<testgroup id = "AENLJA0A1134087010">
<title>
Coolant control valve check
</title>
<test1>
<ptxt>
Check coolant control valve. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLJA0A1636008"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</test1>
<question>
Is check result OK?
</question>
<result type = "yes"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Replace ECM and recheck DTC. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLJA0A1336001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</action>
<result type = "no"/>
<action>
<ptxt>
Replace coolant control valve. 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLJA0A1636007"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</action>
</testgroup>
</diag>
